articles.content_en:
Article 1 Where a civil relation falls under any of the following circumstances, the People's Court may determine that it is a foreign-related civil relation:
(1) one or both parties are foreign citizens, foreign legal persons, other organizations, or stateless persons;
(2) the habitual residence of one or both parties is outside the territory of the People's Republic of China;
(3) the subject matter is outside the territory of the People's Republic of China;
(4) the legal facts that give rise to, alter, or terminate the civil relation occur outside the territory of the People's Republic of China; or
(5) other circumstances under which it may be determined as a foreign-related civil relation.

Article 10 Where any of the following circumstances exists, and the provisions of laws and administrative regulations involve the public interest of the People's Republic of China, cannot be excluded by agreement between the parties, and directly apply to foreign-related civil relations without the guidance of conflict rules, the People's Court shall determine them as compulsory provisions as provided in Article 4 of the Law on the Application of Laws to Foreign-Related Civil Relations:
(1) involving the protection of workers' rights and interests;
(2) involving food or public health safety;
(3) involving environmental safety;
(4) involving financial security such as foreign exchange control;
(5) involving antitrust and anti-dumping; or
(6) other circumstances that shall be determined as compulsory provisions.
